## What is a Goliath Flag Bet
A Goliath Flag is an eight-selection wager consisting of 303 separate bets. The structure combines 247 standard accumulator bets with 28 additional Up-And-Down Single Stakes About (SSA) pairs. Players need at least two winning selections to generate returns, though meaningful profits typically require three or more winners. The Flag variant offers greater coverage than a standard Goliath by including SSA pairs, which create conditional bets where winnings from one selection automatically stake on another.
### Goliath vs Goliath Flag: Key Differences
A standard Goliath contains 247 bets from eight selections: 28 doubles, 56 trebles, 70 four-folds, 56 five-folds, 28 six-folds, 8 seven-folds, and 1 eight-fold. The Goliath Flag adds 28 Up-And-Down SSA pairs to this foundation, bringing the total to 303 bets. SSA pairs function as conditional doubles—if the first selection wins, stakes and returns carry forward to the second selection, then reverse. This creates two-way coverage between specific selection pairings. The additional 28 SSA pairs increase total cost by approximately 11% compared to a standard Goliath but provide enhanced return potential when multiple selections win. The Goliath Flag Calculator automatically factors these SSA pairs into total cost and return projections.
